{
  "project": "xschema-docs",
  "description": "Twoslash Integration - Show autocomplete, type inference, and error prevention in docs using real generated code",
  "phase2": {
    "description": "Polish and fix issues from phase 1",
    "userStories": [
      {
        "title": "Reduce hover noise in Quick Start (index.mdx)",
        "description": "As a reader, I want only meaningful things to be hoverable so I can focus on what matters.",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "Only these identifiers should have ^? annotations showing types: profileSchema, result",
          "Imports (createXSchemaClient, schemas) should not be distracting",
          "Consider using simpler client helper pattern (like adapter pages) instead of full @xschemadev/client types",
          "Typecheck passes",
          "Verify in browser - only key variables show type popups"
        ],
        "passes": false,
        "notes": "Currently too many things are hoverable. Simplify virtual types and focus annotations on what matters."
      },
      {
        "title": "Reduce hover noise in typescript.mdx client setup",
        "description": "As a reader, I want only meaningful things to be hoverable so I can focus on what matters.",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "Only these identifiers should have ^? annotations: profileSchema, safeParse result, parsed properties (id, email)",
          "createXSchemaClient, schemas, xschema should not have prominent type hovers",
          "Simplify virtual type setup to reduce noise",
          "Typecheck passes",
          "Verify in browser"
        ],
        "passes": false,
        "notes": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Show actual compile error for type-only example",
        "description": "As a reader, when the docs say 'this would be a compile error', I want to see the actual error.",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "In typescript.mdx 'Type-only' section, use @errors annotation to show the actual compile error",
          "The error should appear when trying to call xschema() when no runtime validator exists",
          "Remove the comment '// This would be a compile error - no runtime validator' and replace with actual error display",
          "Typecheck passes",
          "Verify in browser - red error text is visible"
        ],
        "passes": false,
        "notes": "Currently just a comment. Should use twoslash @errors annotation to show real error."
      },
      {
        "title": "Fix Effect adapter type inference",
        "description": "As a reader viewing the Effect adapter page, I want to see the actual parsed type, not 'unknown'.",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "User variable shows actual object type { id: string; email: string; name?: string | undefined } or similar",
          "NOT showing 'unknown' which is current behavior",
          "Virtual type definitions properly model Effect Schema type inference",
          "Typecheck passes",
          "Verify in browser at /docs/adapters/effect"
        ],
        "passes": true,
        "notes": "Virtual types use `declare const User: S.Schema<{ id: string; email: string; name?: string }>` which properly models the type parameter. The decodeUnknownSync generic extracts A from Schema<A, I, R> correctly. Type popup shows { id: string; email: string; name?: string }."
      },
      {
        "title": "Fix Valibot adapter type inference",
        "description": "As a reader viewing the Valibot adapter page, I want to see the actual parsed type, not 'unknown'.",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "User variable shows actual object type { id: string; email: string; name?: string | undefined } with index signature",
          "NOT showing 'unknown'",
          "Virtual type definitions properly model Valibot's InferOutput pattern",
          "The v.pipe() call must preserve type through the chain, not lose it to unknown",
          "Typecheck passes",
          "Verify in browser at /docs/adapters/valibot"
        ],
        "passes": true,
        "notes": "Fixed by changing pipe() generic from `pipe<T>(...args: unknown[]): BaseSchema<T>` to `pipe<A, B, C extends BaseSchema<unknown>>(a: A, b: B, c: C): C` which extracts the return type from the last argument. Also inlined the InferEntries type alias into looseObject to get cleaner type display."
      }
    ]
  },
  "userStories": [
    {
      "title": "Create shared example schemas",
      "description": "As a developer, I need source JSON Schemas that all adapter examples will use for both simple and multi-namespace demos.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Create web/examples/schemas/user.schema.json with id (string), name (string, optional), email (string format email)",
        "Create web/examples/schemas/app.schema.json with theme (string enum: light/dark), language (string), debug (boolean, optional)",
        "Both schemas are valid JSON Schema draft-2020-12",
        "Typecheck passes"
      ],
      "passes": true,
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "title": "Create Zod example and generate",
      "description": "As a developer, I need Zod generated code with multiple namespaces for Twoslash to import.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Create web/examples/typescript/zod/xschema.jsonc with two schemas",
        "First schema: namespace 'user', id 'Profile', source ../../schemas/user.schema.json",
        "Second schema: namespace 'app', id 'Config', source ../../schemas/app.schema.json",
        "Both use @xschemadev/zod adapter",
        "Run xschema generate in that directory",
        "Commit generated web/examples/typescript/zod/.xschema/xschema.gen.ts",
        "Generated file exports schemas with keys 'user:Profile' and 'app:Config'",
        "Typecheck passes"
      ],
      "passes": true,
      "notes": "Used two config files (user.xschema.jsonc, app.xschema.jsonc) since xschema namespace is per-file. Generated output manually via adapter CLI since packages aren't on npm yet."
    },
    {
